# Enterprise auth requests for UML-MCP + Microsoft Entra ID.
# Works with VS Code "REST Client" and JetBrains HTTP Client. Copy values into an
# http-client.env.json / .env; never commit real secrets or tokens.
# Docs: docs/enterprise/README.md

@baseUrl = https://mcp.contoso.com
@mcpUrl = {{baseUrl}}/mcp
@tenantId = 11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555
@apiClientId = aaaaaaaa-bbbb-cccc-dddd-eeeeeeeeeeee
@daemonClientId = <app-only-client-id>
@daemonClientSecret = <app-only-client-secret>
@login = https://login.microsoftonline.com

### 1. Protected resource metadata (RFC 9728) — public, 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp
Accept: application/json

### 2. No token → 401 + WWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata="…", scope="…"
POST {{mcpUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list"}

### 3. Entra OpenID Connect discovery (v2) — note: no code_challenge_methods_supported
GET {{login}}/{{tenantId}}/v2.0/.well-known/openid-configuration

### 4. App-only token (client credentials, OAuth 2.0) — needs app role MCP.Write.All
# @name appToken
POST {{login}}/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials
&client_id={{daemonClientId}}
&client_secret={{daemonClientSecret}}
&scope=api://{{apiClientId}}/.default

### 5. Call MCP with the app-only token → 200
POST {{mcpUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{appToken.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/list"}

### 6. Generate (needs write) → 200 with MCP.Write.All, 403 insufficient_scope with read only
POST {{mcpUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{appToken.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"generate_uml","arguments":{"diagram_type":"mermaid","code":"graph TD; A-->B","output_format":"svg"}}}

### 7. Token in the query string is refused → 400 invalid_request
POST {{mcpUrl}}?access_token=not-allowed
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"ping"}

### 8. Token for another service (Microsoft Graph audience) → 401 invalid_audience
# Get one with: az account get-access-token --resource-type ms-graph --query accessToken -o tsv
POST {{mcpUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer <graph-token>
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"method":"ping"}

### 9. entra-proxy mode: authorization server metadata (RFC 8414) — S256 only
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server

### 10. entra-proxy mode: dynamic client registration (RFC 7591) → 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/oauth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"client_name":"REST client test","redirect_uris":["http://127.0.0.1:8765/callback"],"token_endpoint_auth_method":"none","grant_types":["authorization_code","refresh_token"],"response_types":["code"]}

### 11. entra-proxy mode: PKCE plain is refused (redirect with error=invalid_request)
GET {{baseUrl}}/oauth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=<client_id>&redirect_uri=http://127.0.0.1:8765/callback&code_challenge=abc&code_challenge_method=plain&state=x

### 12. Unknown path → 404 (never an auth challenge)
GET {{baseUrl}}/mcpx
